# 1. DOCUMENT PURPOSE

## 1.1 Objective

This document defines the approved target system architecture for MOMENT.

It establishes the architectural boundaries, application layers, infrastructure, service responsibilities, data flows, integration patterns, security boundaries, realtime architecture and deployment model required to transform MOMENT into a production-ready application.

The document is an implementation contract for the engineering team and AI coding agents.

It must be used alongside the MOMENT Master PRD.

## 1.2 Architectural principle

MOMENT must be developed as a modular monolith with clearly separated business domains.

The application must remain straightforward to develop, test, deploy and maintain without introducing unnecessary distributed-system complexity.

The architecture must support future expansion without requiring an early migration to microservices.

## 1.3 Important implementation rule

This document defines the target architecture, not an assumption that the existing prototype already follows it.

Before implementation, inspect the current repository and infrastructure.

If the existing implementation differs from this target:

1. Document the difference.
2. Determine whether the existing implementation is functional and secure.
3. Identify the migration cost and risks.
4. Propose the required change.
5. Obtain approval for material architectural changes.
6. Implement progressively.

Never replace a working implementation simply to match a preferred folder structure or architectural pattern.

