# 6. MODULE BOUNDARIES AND DEPENDENCIES

The following dependency rules are mandatory.

1. Presentation components may call approved application interfaces.
2. Presentation components must not directly execute privileged database operations.
3. Domain modules must not depend on UI components.
4. Database queries must be isolated in data-access functions.
5. Shared validation schemas may be reused across trusted application boundaries.
6. Modules must not directly modify another module's internal records without an approved interface or documented transaction.
7. Cross-module operations must use explicit application services.
8. Circular dependencies must be avoided.

Example:

A user reacting to a post follows this path:

```text
Post Interaction Component
        |
        v
POST /api/v1/posts/{postId}/reactions
        |
        v
Authentication Verification
        |
        v
Request Validation
        |
        v
Social Domain Service
        |
        v
Reaction Persistence
        |
        v
PostgreSQL
        |
        v
Response / Realtime Update
        |
        v
Updated User Interface
```

