# 12. API ARCHITECTURE

## 12.1 API conventions

Application APIs use the versioned prefix:

`/api/v1`

Endpoints must be grouped by business domain.

Examples:

```text
/api/v1/profiles
/api/v1/discovery
/api/v1/posts
/api/v1/posts/{postId}/comments
/api/v1/posts/{postId}/reactions
/api/v1/polls
/api/v1/polls/{pollId}/votes
/api/v1/games
/api/v1/games/{gameId}/sessions
/api/v1/communities
/api/v1/notifications
/api/v1/reports
/api/v1/admin
```

Exact request and response contracts belong in Document 04.

## 12.2 API responsibilities

The API layer must:

- Validate requests.
- Authenticate requests.
- Enforce permissions.
- Call domain services.
- Handle transactions.
- Return predictable responses.
- Avoid leaking internal exceptions.
- Apply rate limits.
- Support request tracing.

## 12.3 Error handling

All APIs must use a consistent error format.

The standard contract will be established in Document 04.

Errors must not reveal:

- Database credentials.
- Internal SQL statements.
- Authentication tokens.
- Stack traces to public clients.
- Private user information.

