# 13. STORAGE ARCHITECTURE

Supabase Storage is the approved storage platform for supported file uploads.

MVP storage must only support approved file types and use cases.

The implementation must define:

- Bucket ownership.
- Access permissions.
- Upload validation.
- File-size restrictions.
- File-type restrictions.
- File naming.
- Deletion lifecycle.
- Public versus private access.
- Signed URL behaviour where applicable.

Do not introduce image or audio posting into the MVP merely because storage is available.

All upload restrictions must be defined in the UI/UX and security specifications before enabling a new upload workflow.

